{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ecom Platform (auth + ecom-api via nginx)",
    "description": "End-to-end collection for the microservices platform via the nginx gateway at {{baseUrl}} (default http://localhost:3008).\n\nAUTH IS PASSWORDLESS (OTP) — signup and login are the SAME flow:\n  1. POST /auth/otp {email}  -> emails a 6-digit code via Mailpit (no token yet); response.isNewUser tells the frontend to show an optional name/mobile form\n  2. Read the code from Mailpit ({{mailpitUrl}}, default http://localhost:8028)\n  3. POST /auth/verify-otp {email,otp,name?,mobile?}  -> creates the account if new, returns the token\n\nThis collection uses BEARER tokens throughout (token in the JSON body, saved to {{accessToken}}). Bearer requests are CSRF-EXEMPT, so no X-CSRF-Token is needed anywhere here. Cookie delivery is shown ONCE — see the 'Cookie mode example' — where CSRF DOES apply: cookie-mode POST/PATCH/DELETE must send `X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}` (that request saves it) or you get 403.\n\nRun order: 1. Request OTP -> 2. Read OTP from Mailpit -> 3. Verify OTP (bearer) -> 4-7 account management -> Ecom API (Profile / products).\n\nAuthenticated account routes (Bearer): GET /auth/me, PATCH /auth/profile, and a 3-step email change: POST /auth/email/change (OTP to OLD email) -> verify-old {newEmail, otp} (OTP to NEW email) -> verify-new {otp} (switch).\n\nDemo admin (seeded): admin@example.com (sign in with an OTP — no password).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3008", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "mailpitUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8028", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "admin@example.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "otp", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "csrfToken", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Gateway",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Gateway health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/gateway/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["gateway", "health"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth service",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Request OTP (signup or login)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('OTP required (no token yet)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.data.otpRequired).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(json.data.accessToken).to.be.undefined;",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('isNewUser =', json.data.isNewUser);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('email', JSON.parse(pm.request.body.raw).email);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@example.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "otp"]
            },
            "description": "Step 1 (passwordless): emails a 6-digit OTP (captured by Mailpit). Same endpoint whether the email is new (signup) or existing (login); response.isNewUser tells the UI whether to show the optional name/mobile form. No token is returned."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Read OTP from Mailpit",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const msg = (json.messages && json.messages[0]) || {};",
                  "const hay = (msg.Subject || '') + ' ' + (msg.Snippet || '');",
                  "const m = hay.match(/(\\d{6})/);",
                  "pm.test('found an OTP in the latest email', () => pm.expect(m, 'no 6-digit code found').to.not.be.null);",
                  "if (m) { pm.collectionVariables.set('otp', m[1]); console.log('OTP =', m[1]); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{mailpitUrl}}/api/v1/messages?limit=1",
              "host": ["{{mailpitUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "messages"],
              "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "1" }]
            },
            "description": "Reads the latest captured email from Mailpit and extracts the 6-digit OTP into {{otp}}. (In a real app the user reads this from their inbox.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Verify OTP (bearer) — saves token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('token issued', () => pm.expect(json.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);",
                  "if (json.data.refreshToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.data.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "verify-otp"]
            },
            "description": "Step 2: exchanges the OTP for a token. Default (bearer) returns the token in the body; the script saves it to {{accessToken}}. For a NEW email you may also send optional \"name\" and \"mobile\" fields to fill the profile at signup."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Get me (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the current user. Uses the Bearer token from step 3."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Update profile (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Admin User\",\n  \"mobile\": \"+15551234567\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/profile",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "profile"]
            },
            "description": "Updates the optional name / mobile (both optional)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Change email - request OTP (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/email/change",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "email", "change"]
            },
            "description": "Step 1 of an email change: no body needed — just emails an OTP to the CURRENT address (proves control of the existing inbox). The new email is supplied at the next step. Then run '2. Read OTP from Mailpit' to capture {{otp}}."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Change email - verify OLD (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"newEmail\": \"admin-new@example.com\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify-old",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "email", "verify-old"]
            },
            "description": "Step 2: supply the NEW email plus the OTP sent to the OLD one (run '2. Read OTP from Mailpit' first to load {{otp}}). On success the server saves newEmail as pending and emails a SECOND OTP to the NEW address. No switch yet."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Change email - verify NEW (Bearer)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.accessToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify-new",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "email", "verify-new"]
            },
            "description": "Step 3: confirms the OTP sent to the NEW email (run '2. Read OTP from Mailpit' again to load the newer {{otp}}), switches the email, and re-issues the token — the script saves the fresh {{accessToken}}."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "9. Delete account - request OTP (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/account/delete",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "account", "delete"]
            },
            "description": "Step 1: emails an OTP to the current address to confirm this destructive, irreversible action. Then run '2. Read OTP from Mailpit'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "10. Delete account - verify (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/account/delete/verify",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "account", "delete", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Step 2: confirms the OTP and soft-deletes (deactivates) the account. The email is freed for a fresh signup; old data is retained under deleted_email. Clears the cookie; the current token stops working on auth routes."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cookie mode example (X-Auth-Source: cookie) — saves CSRF",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// In cookie mode the server sets a readable csrf_token cookie AND",
                  "// returns csrfToken in the body. Save it so cookie-mode state-changing",
                  "// requests can send it as the X-CSRF-Token header.",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const csrf = (json.data && json.data.csrfToken) || pm.cookies.get('csrf_token');",
                  "if (csrf) pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', csrf);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Auth-Source", "value": "cookie" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "verify-otp"]
            },
            "description": "THE single cookie example. Everything else here uses Bearer (which is CSRF-exempt). To use cookie delivery, add `X-Auth-Source: cookie` to any token-issuing request: the server sets HttpOnly access/refresh cookies + a readable csrf_token cookie (also returned as data.csrfToken). Postman auto-sends the cookies afterward, so you can drop the Authorization header.\n\nCSRF: for cookie-mode STATE-CHANGING calls (POST/PATCH/DELETE) you MUST also send the header `X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}` (this request's test script saves it). GET is exempt; bearer requests are exempt. Without it you get 403. (Re-run Request OTP + Read OTP first; each OTP is single-use.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh token (rotates) — saves new tokens",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.accessToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.data.accessToken);",
                  "if (json.data && json.data.refreshToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.data.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Swaps a refresh token for a fresh access token WITHOUT re-doing the OTP flow. Single-use: the presented refresh token is rotated (revoked) and a new one issued — the script saves both. Reusing the old one returns 401. (Cookie clients omit the body; the token is read from the HttpOnly refresh cookie.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout (revokes refresh token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes the presented refresh token and clears both auth cookies. Cookie clients can omit the body."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout all devices (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout-all"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes EVERY active session for the current user. All existing refresh tokens stop working."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "JWKS (public keys)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks.json",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": [".well-known", "jwks.json"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ecom API",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health (public)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List products (public)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/products",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "products"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Profile (Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/profile",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "profile"]
            },
            "description": "Uses the Bearer token from 'Verify OTP (bearer)'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create product (admin, Bearer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Cap\",\n  \"priceCents\": 1500,\n  \"stock\": 40\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/products",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "products"]
            },
            "description": "Requires an ADMIN token. Log in as admin and verify OTP first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create product WITHOUT auth (expect 401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('rejected with 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Auth-Source", "value": "bearer" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Hacker Hat\",\n  \"priceCents\": 1,\n  \"stock\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/products",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "products"]
            },
            "description": "Negative test — forces bearer source with no Authorization header -> 401."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
